From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mingyu Lei <leimy@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 07:02:54 -0700
Subject: FSA: Block ~/.cache on all platforms in sensitive path blocklist

GenerateBlockPaths() only blocked ~/.cache via base::DIR_CACHE under
IS_LINUX, IS_CHROMEOS, and IS_ANDROID. On macOS, base::DIR_CACHE
resolves to ~/Library/Caches, and on Windows base::DIR_CACHE does not
exist, leaving ~/.cache unblocked under base::DIR_HOME
(kDontBlockChildren) despite cross-platform tools storing virtual
environments, package caches, and tokens there. On Linux and ChromeOS,
~/.cache was also left unblocked when $XDG_CACHE_HOME pointed
elsewhere, or for secondary signed-in profiles on ChromeOS.

Add a platform-independent BlockPath::CreateRelative(base::DIR_HOME,
".cache", kBlockAllChildren) rule alongside ~/.config, and keep the
base::DIR_CACHE rule on Linux, ChromeOS, and Android to cover custom
$XDG_CACHE_HOME locations and Android's app cache directory.

Bug: 577400245
Test: unit_tests --gtest_filter=*FileSystemAccessPermissionContext*
Change-Id: I49709818791a0280ccaf6bb89e12127f87191c52
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8668442
Commit-Queue: Anna Sato <annasato@chromium.org>
Auto-Submit: Mingyu Lei <leimy@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Anna Sato <annasato@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1729091}

Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y):
Electron's refactor_expose_file_system_access_blocklist.patch moves GenerateBlockPaths() from chrome_file_system_access_permission_context.cc into the header on this branch, so the new ~/.cache kBlockAllChildren rule was applied to the kBlockPaths table in chrome_file_system_access_permission_context.h instead of the .cc. This branch has no Linux/ChromeOS base::DIR_CACHE rule yet (only the Android one), so the comment-only change to that rule has no counterpart. The unit test hunk applied unchanged.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/file_system_access/chrome_file_system_access_permission_context.h b/chrome/browser/file_system_access/chrome_file_system_access_permission_context.h
index 2b9f609951486486e6b446fc3bf135efed560113..85c9249ac7450e2debb8406c339db3c1369b1ec8 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/file_system_access/chrome_file_system_access_permission_context.h
+++ b/chrome/browser/file_system_access/chrome_file_system_access_permission_context.h
@@ -586,6 +586,10 @@ class ChromeFileSystemAccessPermissionContext
         // it on all platforms, see crbug.com/569012015.
         BlockPath::CreateRelative(base::DIR_HOME, FILE_PATH_LITERAL(".config"),
                                   BlockType::kBlockAllChildren),
+        // ~/.cache holds caches and virtual environments for cross-platform
+        // tools, so block it on all platforms, see crbug.com/577400245.
+        BlockPath::CreateRelative(base::DIR_HOME, FILE_PATH_LITERAL(".cache"),
+                                  BlockType::kBlockAllChildren),
         // Shell startup files in the home directory, including the ones read by
         // Git Bash on Windows, see crbug.com/558362029.
         BlockPath::CreateRelative(base::DIR_HOME,
